{"id": "EUVD-2026-75021", "enisaUuid": "5d2161aa-6575-3509-ac6d-c95b16366abb", "description": "zstd-jni before 1.5.7-14 performs 32-bit signed bounds checks on three direct-ByteBuffer frame-size native methods, allowing out-of-bounds memory reads via negative or overflowing offsets. Attackers can supply negative offset values near Integer.MIN_VALUE to read unmapped memory, causing JVM termination or extracting arbitrary frame size data from unintended memory locations.", "datePublished": "2026-09-09T14:32:43", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-09T16:13:14", "baseScore": 8.8, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:L/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/luben/zstd-jni/security/advisories/GHSA-jfr6-9xqw-2g2q", "https://github.com/luben/zstd-jni/commit/d7a1c99322d5e1fc71932e722c0b5bb2fc525d3f", "https://github.com/luben/zstd-jni/blob/v1.5.7-13/src/main/native/jni_zstd.c", "https://github.com/luben/zstd-jni/blob/v1.5.7-13/src/main/java/com/github/luben/zstd/Zstd.java", "https://github.com/luben/zstd-jni/releases/tag/v1.5.7-14", "https://github.com/luben/zstd-jni/commit/46dcb2a54c8b8f2ce2cad7187a7513f509c533ac", "https://github.com/luben/zstd-jni", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/zstd-jni-1.1.1-through-1.5.7-13-out-of-bounds-read-via-direct-bytebuffer-frame-size-methods"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-87823", "GHSA-cm3p-487m-cmvq"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.43, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "7fcb895e-37e1-388f-9c47-2599a3248c66", "product": {"name": "zstd-jni", "vendor": {"name": "luben"}}, "product_version": "1.1.1 <1.5.7-14"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "75702fe7-11f9-3e0d-a1aa-fa49ce51e5ba", "vendor": {"name": "luben"}}], "isExploited": false}